# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the pitch fee doubles (pairs D3b)

== the pitch fee doubles
tier: life event
sphere: comm
haunt: comm.market
ladder: known
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-80
per_year: 0 0 .002 .004 .004 .002
drivers: harsh+.2 prosper-.2 unrest+.1
times: Market and street traders face rising pitch fees and rents; a fee rise that threatens one's own stall comes to about 1 in 12 lives, nearly all of them market traders (estimate). The superstore's coming is 'the superstore on the ring road' (ready/ev-comm)
likelier: a market sold to a private owner, a town centre being rebuilt, a trader on thin margins
rarer: a market run by the council on fixed fees, a person who never trades
gap: 5-20
tone: trouble
life: work, money, community
horizon: months
roles: colleague
who: colleague
earth: the market's new owners double the pitch fee from next month, and the stall you have kept for years no longer pays
scene: The notice is taped to every stall by seven: the market has new owners, and from next month the pitch fee doubles. {N} does the sums on the back of the notice. At the new fee the stall barely pays.
scene W: The old fee was set by the council in the open. Nobody asked the stallholders about this one.
scene U: {N} can see the plan behind it: empty the market, then sell the site.
scene B: Half the stallholders will fold. Whoever stays will have the market to themselves.
scene R: {N} wants to tear the notice down and throw it on the brazier.
scene G: {colleague} at the next stall has been there forty years, and is already packing up, slowly.
