- U | find out who bought the market, and what they mean to build on it | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: comm.U | chance: 60
- B | offer to take the empty pitches at the old rate, and wait the owners out | v: power, achievement | sphere: comm.B | chance: 60
- R | take the stall on the road to the fair towns, and leave the market behind | v: stimulation, self-direction | lever: exit | sphere: comm.R | chance: 60
- G | stay on at the new fee for the regulars who have bought from you for years | act: stay on at the new fee for the regulars who have bought from them for years | v: tradition, security | lever: loyalty | sphere: comm.G | chance: 60
- WB | ask the lawyer two stalls down to read the old lease for a clause they broke | v: conformity, power | sphere: comm.WB | chance: 50
- WG | start a stallholders' co-op, and run your own market in the church car park | act: start a stallholders' co-op, and run their own market in the church car park | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: found | sphere: comm.GW | chance: 50
- UR | sell online through the week, and from the van at the market gate on Saturdays | v: self-direction, stimulation | tech: internet | sphere: comm.UR | chance: 50
- UG | share one pitch with the old neighbour, splitting the fee and the days | v: benevolence, security | sphere: comm.GU | chance: 50
- BR | sell off the stock at one great last market, and start again elsewhere | v: stimulation, achievement | lever: exit | sphere: comm.BR | chance: 50
works: The stallholders hold together, and the council caps the fee for three years.
works: {N} finds a better pitch in a market two towns away, and the takings there are higher within a season.
fails: Half the market is empty by the spring, and with the crowds gone {Ns} stall fades with it.
fails: {N} hangs on for a year at the new fee, then gives up the pitch with nothing saved.

