earth: a buyer for a chain of shops tastes your sauce at the trade fair, and offers an order ten times bigger than any you have filled
scene: At the trade fair a buyer for a chain of shops tries {Ns} sauce at the stand, then offers an order ten times bigger than any {N} has filled. The contract can be signed on the spot, at a price {N} must meet every month for three years.
scene W: The terms are fair on paper, and {N} means to keep every one of them, which means knowing first whether that can be done.
scene U: Ten times the order means ten times the tomatoes, a bigger kitchen and staff. {N} starts the sums at once.
scene B: This is the deal that turns a kitchen into a firm. {N} means to get the best terms out of it.
scene R: {N} wants to shout, hug the buyer, and say yes before the buyer can think twice.
scene G: The sauce is an old family recipe, made with the neighbours' tomatoes. {N} wonders who it is for, ten times over.
