earth: the mechanic lifts your second-hand car and shows you the rust painted over and the mileage turned back: the seller knew
scene: The car was a bargain, bought for cash from a man on the other side of town. Three weeks later the mechanic lifts it up and shows {N} the rust painted over and the mileage turned back. The seller knew.
scene W: {N} shook the man's hand on it. A handshake is meant to mean something.
scene U: {N} goes back over every word of the sale, looking for the question that should have been asked.
scene B: {N} paid in cash. The man knows it, and probably thinks {N} will just let it go.
scene R: {N} wants to drive straight round there and have it out on his doorstep.
scene G: {friend} bought a car from the same man last year. {N} wonders how many others he has done this to.
